<title>FRANCE: Pechiney 1996 loss 2.98 billion francs.</title>
<headline>Pechiney 1996 loss 2.98 billion francs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable		 loss    2,977  vs  profit 1,465</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		    3.30   vs	   same</p>
<p>    Operating			  loss    2,018  vs  profit 2,985</p>
<p>    Turnover				    64,372  vs	  68,687</p>
<p>NOTE - Pechiney gave the result in a statement. It said restructuring provisions totalled 3.69 billion francs, of which 2.278 billion were for the Challenge project and 1.412 billion for risk. The latter amount includes 531 million to cover a judgment in the National Can case which went against Pechiney.  </p>
<p>Net debt totalled 14.775 billion francs versus 14.295 billion.</p>
<p>Net financial charges were 991 million versus 1.805 billion.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsrooom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
